ivery and pricing validation. The functionality is formally documented and referenced in the official SAP release notes, confirming its integration into the platform's core operations. This development supports better alignment between sales, finance, and operations teams in managing solution-based contracts and pricing models. [Data: Sources (1), Date_Range ((2023, 01, 01), (2025, 09, 23))]\n\n## Joule Supports Fetching Solution Quotation Information Based on Input Criteria\n\nJoule enables users to retrieve detailed information about solution quotations using predefined input criteria, allowing for targeted and efficient data retrieval. This feature supports dynamic querying of quotation data, which is essential for auditing, compliance, and performance analysis. By enabling users to filter and retrieve specific quotation records, Joule improves transparency and access to pricing data across departments. This functionality is particularly valuable in environments where multiple stakeholders need to review or validate quotation details in real time. The capability is explicitly stated as being available from the 2023 FPS01 release and is maintained through the latest revision in 2025. This supports data-driven decision-making and strengthens the traceability of solution pricing decisions. [Data: Sources (1), Date_Range ((2023, 01, 01), (2025, 09, 23))]\n\n## Expansion of Joule to SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition with Condition Records for Pricing\n\nIn addition to private edition capabilities, Joule has been extended to SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition, where it now enables users to view business data related to condition records for pricing in sales. This expansion broadens the reach of Joule’s functionality to a wider user base, including public cloud customers who rely on SAP’s cloud-based solutions. The ability to access condition records—such as pricing conditions, discounts, and surcharges—provides deeper visibility into pricing logic and supports more accurate sales forecasting and contract management. This integration is part of a broader trend in SAP to enhance data accessibility and usability across its cloud platforms. The feature is described as being in general availability and valid as of September 23, 2025, indicating it is stable and widely adopted. [Data: Sources (10), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 19), (2025, 09, 23))]\n\n## Joule's Capabilities Are Continuously Updated and Maintained\n\nThe documentation and release history of Joule show a consistent pattern of updates and revisions, with the latest revision recorded on October 20, 2025. This indicates an ongoing development cycle focused on refining functionality, improving usability, and addressing user feedback. The fact that the valid as-of date is set to September 23, 2025, suggests that the current version is the most up-to-date and reliable for operational use. This continuous improvement reflects SAP’s commitment to maintaining a robust and evolving platform that adapts to changing business needs. The updates are categorized as 'new' features and are marked as general availability, indicating they are not experimental but are intended for production use. This stability and evolution make Joule a reliable tool for enterprise operations. [Data: Sources (1), (10), Date_Range ((2023, 01, 01), (2025, 10, 20))]\n\n## Joule's Role in Enhancing Pricing and Sales Operations\n\nJoule plays a central role in improving pricing and sales operations by providing tools to manage solution quotations and access pricing condition records. These capabilities directly support sales teams in finalizing quotes, finance teams in validating pricing, and operations in planning delivery timelines. By integrating quotation management with pricing data, Joule reduces the risk of pricing errors and ensures consistency across sales cycles. This integration is particularly important in complex solution-based environments where multiple pricing rules and conditions apply. The feature set supports both private and public cloud deployments, ensuring scalability and accessibility across different organizational models. This makes Joule a critical enabler of efficient and transparent pricing workflows. [Data: Sources (1), (10), Date_Range ((2023, 01, 01), (2025, 09, 23))]"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_b0f19bfbbe6fc298c3b9def937b8aeac40ddb31355a2c806cc51a743a40c9bb3_v2"}